<title>CHINA: Shanghai Metal Exchange to close for New Year Day.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Metal Exchange to close for New Year Day.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai Metal Exchange will close on Wednesday for the New Year holiday and trading will resume on Thursday, an exchange statement said.</p>
<p>Copper contracts on the exchange rose on Tuesday due to short-covering ahead of the holiday, with the most active April 1997 contract ending up 70 yuan to 20,640 yuan per tonne, traders said.</p>
